## Commits

- **One change per commit**, as small as the change itself. Three unrelated
  edits in one file are three commits.
- Several files touched for one change are one commit; several files each
  changed for their own reason are one commit each.
- Split as fine as the tree still builds at every commit.
- Commit as you go. Progress that is not committed is lost when a turn is
  interrupted.
- **Never** `git add -A` or `git commit -a`. Stage the paths you changed.

---

## Feedforward constraints & Jidoka test gates

To prevent rework loops and maximize first-pass yield ($\ge 90\%$):

1. **Feedforward Context Assembly:** Before starting code generation, identify domain constraints, relevant historical defects from `evidence/rework.md`, and active role boundaries.
2. **Deterministic Pre-Flight Checks:** Run local tests and mechanical gates (`{{TEST_COMMAND}}`) incrementally after every discrete file modification rather than waiting until turn completion.
3. **Automated Stop-on-Defect (Jidoka / Autonomation):** If any mechanical gate or unit test fails, halt new feature generation immediately, isolate root cause, and resolve before proceeding. Do not build new code on top of a failing test.

---

## Branches and other agents

Other sessions may be working in this repository at the same time.

- Never revert, reset, rebase or amend a commit you did not write. Report it
  and wait, or branch off and work there.
- Re-read a file immediately before overwriting it.
- Before calling any work lost, check which branch contains it.
- A sub-agent has its own worktree and branch: its work is there, not on yours.

---

## Mechanical gates

Where a check can be a command, it is a command with a documented return code,
and it runs in CI. Prose judgment is reserved for what a command cannot decide.

| Gate | Command | Refuses |
|---|---|---|
| {{GATE}} | `{{COMMAND}}` | {{WHAT_IT_REFUSES}} |

---

## Claims and evidence

- **No claim without a same-turn receipt.** "Passing", "fixed", "shipped" need
  the tool output that shows it, in the same turn.
- **Never report an identifier you did not read back** — issue numbers, run
  ids, shas, commit trailers.
- If a tool result arrives truncated, any claim resting on the elided region is
  unverified: re-run a targeted check before asserting it.

---

## Secrets

- Never commit credentials. `{{SECRETS_FILE}}` is the only place they live, and
  it is not in this repository.
- Never paste a credential into an issue, a chat, a log or a commit message —
  including in a screenshot.
